mobile-app
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.git

# Local dev env files — must never ship in a deploy. web-app/.env sets
# FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST=127.0.0.1:8080 for local dev; if uploaded, Next.js
# loads it at build time and it silently shadows the real Vercel dashboard
# env vars at runtime, making every Firestore call try to reach a local
# emulator that doesn't exist in production. web-app/.vercelignore already
# has this rule, but it only applies when web-app itself is the deploy
# root — a manual `vercel --prod` run from the repo root (needed because
# the project's configured Root Directory is "web-app", so the CLI must
# upload the full repo) uses *this* file instead.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
